B.3 Role Drift Measurement in Undifferentiated Teams

For undifferentiated teams, role drift is measured using Latent Dirichlet Allocation (LDA) on transcript text. Each utterance is assigned a topic distribution over four latent topics corresponding to the four constraint dimensions. The entropy of each team member's topic distribution over the scenario quantifies their degree of specialization:

H_i = -\sum_{k=1}^4 p_{ik}\log p_{ik},

where $p_{ik}$ is the fraction of member $i$'s utterances assigned to topic $k$. Low entropy indicates strong specialization; high entropy indicates generalist behavior.

